answer:
Step 1: Let the rotation matrix be $ R = \begin{pmatrix} \cos\theta & -\sin\theta \\ \sin\theta & \cos\theta \end{pmatrix} $. The rotation takes $ \begin{pmatrix} 13 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} $ to $ \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix} $, so:
$$
R \begin{pmatrix} 13 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 13\cos\theta \\ 13\sin\theta \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix}
$$

Step 2: Equating components:
$$
13\cos\theta = 5 \Rightarrow \cos\theta = \frac{5}{13}
$$
$$
13\sin\theta = -12 \Rightarrow \sin\theta = -\frac{12}{13}
$$

Step 3: The rotation matrix is:
$$
R = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{5}{13} & -\left(-\frac{12}{13}\right) \\ -\frac{12}{13} & \frac{5}{13} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{5}{13} & \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{12}{13} & \frac{5}{13} \end{pmatrix}
$$

Step 4: Apply $ R $ to $ \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} $:
$$
R \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{5}{13} & \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{12}{13} & \frac{5}{13} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ \frac{5}{13} \end{pmatrix}
$$

\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \dfrac{12}{13} \\ \dfrac{5}{13} \end{pmatrix}}

