answer:
Step 1: The radius of the circle connects the center (3,2) to the point of tangency (5,5). Compute the slope of the radius:  
\[
m_{\text{radius}} = \frac{5 - 2}{5 - 3} = \frac{3}{2}
\]

Step 2: The tangent line at a point on a circle is perpendicular to the radius at that point. The slope of the tangent line is the negative reciprocal of the slope of the radius:  
\[
m_{\text{tangent}} = -\frac{1}{m_{\text{radius}}} = -\frac{1}{\frac{3}{2}} = -\frac{2}{3}
\]

\boxed{-\frac{2}{3}}

