answer:
Step 1: Compute powers of $\mathbf{A}$ to identify a pattern.  
Given:  
$$
\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
$$

Step 2: Compute $\mathbf{A}^2$:  
$$
\mathbf{A}^2 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A} = 
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
$$

Step 3: Compute $\mathbf{A}^3$:  
$$
\mathbf{A}^3 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^2 = 
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
= -\mathbf{A}
$$

Step 4: Compute $\mathbf{A}^4$:  
$$
\mathbf{A}^4 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^3 = \mathbf{A} \cdot (-\mathbf{A}) = -\mathbf{A}^2
= -\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
$$

Step 5: Compute $\mathbf{A}^5$:  
$$
\mathbf{A}^5 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^4 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
= \mathbf{A}
$$

Step 6: Observe the cycle:  
$\mathbf{A}^1 = \mathbf{A}$  
$\mathbf{A}^2 = \mathbf{A}^2$  
$\mathbf{A}^3 = -\mathbf{A}$  
$\mathbf{A}^4 = -\mathbf{A}^2$  
$\mathbf{A}^5 = \mathbf{A}$  
$\mathbf{A}^6 = \mathbf{A}^2$  
So the powers of $\mathbf{A}$ cycle every 4 steps starting from $\mathbf{A}^1$:  
$$
\mathbf{A}^n = 
\begin{cases}
\mathbf{A} & n \equiv 1 \pmod{4} \\
\mathbf{A}^2 & n \equiv 2 \pmod{4} \\
-\mathbf{A} & n \equiv 3 \pmod{4} \\
-\mathbf{A}^2 & n \equiv 0 \pmod{4}
\end{cases}
$$

Step 7: Compute $95 \mod 4$:  
$95 \div 4 = 23$ remainder $3$, so $95 \equiv 3 \pmod{4}$

Step 8: Therefore, $\mathbf{A}^{95} = -\mathbf{A}$

Step 9: Compute $-\mathbf{A}$:  
$$
-\mathbf{A} = -\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}
$$

$$
\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & -1 & 0 \end{pmatrix}}
$$

